I am building a production-ready multi-tenant Broker / Calling Management Software.

Build the system with a clean, scalable architecture. The system must support hierarchical users, strict tenant isolation, role-based permissions, campaign management, Excel lead importing, manual calling, and Preview Auto Dialing.

1. USER HIERARCHY

The system must have the following hierarchy:

SUPER ADMIN
↓
AGENCY
↓
MANAGER
↓
ADMIN
↓
USER

Super Admin

Super Admin is the platform owner.

Super Admin must be able to:

- Create agencies
- Edit agencies
- Activate/deactivate agencies
- Delete agencies where appropriate
- View all agencies
- View agency statistics
- Set limits for each agency
- Manage agency subscription/status
- View all managers, admins, users, campaigns and calling activity
- Have permission to make manual calls
- Have complete system access

When creating an agency, Super Admin must be able to configure limits such as:

- Maximum Managers
- Maximum Admins
- Maximum Users

Example:

Agency: ABC Finance

Manager Limit: 10
Admin Limit: 30
User Limit: 300

The system must enforce these limits at backend level.

Example:

Managers: 10/10
Admins: 28/30
Users: 287/300

If an agency reaches its limit, it must not be able to create additional accounts until the limit is increased.

---

2. AGENCY

Each agency is a separate tenant.

Agency data must be completely isolated from other agencies.

Agency must be able to manage resources only within its own tenant.

Agency should be able to:

- View its managers
- Create/manage managers within the allocated limit
- View admins
- View users
- View campaigns
- View calling activity according to permissions
- View usage statistics

Agency must never be able to access another agency's data.

---

3. MANAGER

A Manager belongs to one Agency.

Manager must be able to create/manage Admins and Users under their own hierarchy according to the limits and permissions assigned to them.

Example:

Manager: Amit

Admin Limit: 5
User Limit: 50

Dashboard should show:

Admins: 5/5
Users: 43/50

Manager must be able to:

- Create Admins
- Edit Admins
- Activate/deactivate Admins
- Create Users
- Edit Users
- Activate/deactivate Users
- Assign users/admins according to permissions
- View relevant campaigns
- View relevant call activity
- Make manual calls

Manager must never access data belonging to another manager/agency unless explicitly permitted.

---

4. ADMIN

Admin belongs to a Manager and therefore to an Agency.

Admin should primarily manage calling campaigns and leads.

Admin must be able to:

- Create campaigns
- Edit campaigns
- Activate/deactivate campaigns
- Upload Excel files
- Import leads
- View imported leads
- Manage leads
- Assign leads/campaigns to users
- Configure calling strategy
- View calling reports
- View call logs
- Export data if permission is granted
- Make manual calls
- Start/manage Preview Auto Dial campaigns

Admin can create unlimited campaigns unless a separate campaign limit is configured.

Example:

Admin
├── Campaign A
├── Campaign B
├── Campaign C
└── Campaign D

---

5. USER

User is the calling agent.

User must be able to:

- Login
- View assigned campaigns/leads
- Make manual calls if permission is enabled
- Use Preview Auto Dial
- View customer/lead information
- Enter call disposition
- Add notes
- Schedule callback
- View relevant call history
- End/save calls properly

Users must only see the campaigns/leads assigned to them.

