15. MULTI-TENANT SECURITY

This is extremely important.

The application must be strictly multi-tenant.

Every major entity must have tenant ownership.

Conceptually:

Agency
↓
Manager
↓
Admin
↓
Campaign
↓
Lead
↓
CallLog

Agency A must NEVER be able to access:

- Agency B users
- Agency B admins
- Agency B managers
- Agency B campaigns
- Agency B leads
- Agency B call logs

Do not rely only on frontend filtering.

Tenant isolation must be enforced at backend/API/database query level.

Every API endpoint must verify:

1. Authentication
2. User role
3. Permission
4. Agency/tenant ownership
5. Object-level access

Prevent IDOR/insecure direct object reference vulnerabilities.

